                            {
                                "target_word": "Löß",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3be30678-e984-3886-b672-4061a01ca2c4",
                                        "entry_id": "08d4033f-6449-3dd4-be92-5f091f116b05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "schluffiges Sedimentgestein, das aus der Zerstörung anderer Gesteine, deren Verwehung und Ablagerung entstanden ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf18f010-672c-4776-98d8-a94ef7bec3c9",
                                                "sense_id": "3be30678-e984-3886-b672-4061a01ca2c4",
                                                "text": "„Die Erkelenzer Börde, Teil des südlichen Niederrheins zwischen Köln und Aachen, hat fruchtbare Böden. Doch leider, leider liegt unter dem Löß Braunkohle.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "521bcb01-ddb6-4119-aa98-e6cddc0199a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4033b69-01ac-38c3-8450-e25a8aa8ac7d",
                        "source_sense_id": "2fcb3c8a-c41d-3624-8714-b70837702f13",
                        "target_lang_word": "loess",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loess",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8aa100c-910e-35f4-a78c-284793e1fcf1",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c479dd-9650-3617-bfac-e83e0842ef30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any sediment, dominated by silt, of eolian (wind-blown) origin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d29cdbe6-c31b-44dc-93d5-ca7a63206cbd",
                                                "sense_id": "f8aa100c-910e-35f4-a78c-284793e1fcf1",
                                                "text": "The Yellow River got its name from the massive amount of fertile loess (yellow earth) which it has deposited in the wheat-growing North China Plain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba3f4c38-ea07-4eb1-ad76-e05edf652a8d",
                                                "sense_id": "f8aa100c-910e-35f4-a78c-284793e1fcf1",
                                                "text": "They blast their sand westwards across the steppe, coating the foothills of the Brooks Range in an icing-sugar dust of the loose, windblown sand-silt mixture known as loess."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b7418ae-af5b-43f7-830a-3c1aa03eea38",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4033b69-01ac-38c3-8450-e25a8aa8ac7d",
                        "source_sense_id": "2fcb3c8a-c41d-3624-8714-b70837702f13",
                        "target_lang_word": "löss",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "löss",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c6bcd69-8ef4-3f3d-a9dd-3928a4806bbe",
                                        "entry_id": "31c457d5-99c2-351d-b126-896a2c68ba1e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of loess."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50da4950-0292-45a1-ba63-69e67bc61c5f",
                                                "sense_id": "1c6bcd69-8ef4-3f3d-a9dd-3928a4806bbe",
                                                "text": "All those tracts of löss which occur within the valleys proper come under the designation of valley-löss, while the term “hill-löss” is applied to those masses which are less closely connected with the valleys, and sometimes extend over plateaux and hilly ground between separate drainage-areas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c728dfb9-0f36-42cd-911c-e658f9f23cac",
                                                "sense_id": "1c6bcd69-8ef4-3f3d-a9dd-3928a4806bbe",
                                                "text": "Among the mountains of middle Germany, and along the north border, there have been found two distinct deposits of löss separated by a weathered zone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ce7f693-4c63-4a18-bdbd-07d4b3b9b6c0",
                                                "sense_id": "1c6bcd69-8ef4-3f3d-a9dd-3928a4806bbe",
                                                "text": "In northern China, the Löss Plateau dates back at least two million years and consists of alternating layers of löss and soil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
